# Authority Model

@bootstrap.authority

Purpose:
  Define what the AI can and cannot do within this project.
  Authority is checked before any executing action.

can:
    read-code
    modify-code
    run-tests
    create-tasks
    propose-skills
    modify: current task scope
    modify: current domain

cannot:
    change-global-rules
    approve-production
    modify-security-policy
    modify: other domains
    modify: external systems

## Check Chain

  TASK
    ↓ requires
  CAPABILITY
    ↓ maps to
  PERMISSION
    ↓ authorizes
  RESOURCE
    ↓ invokes
  TOOL

AI MUST resolve this chain before every tool invocation.

## Examples

@example.auth-check

  Task T2041:
    requires: write:file

  Authority resolution:
    write:file → @permission.file-write
    permission.file-write → authorized for current task scope
    ALLOW

@example.auth-blocked

  Task T9901:
    requires: production-database

  Authority resolution:
    production-database → NOT in can list
    BLOCKED

## Authority Sources

Authority is derived from:
  1. .sdd/bootstrap/authority.sdd (this file)
  2. .sdd/project/sdd-rules.sdd (project-specific constraints)
  3. .sdd/tasks/T2041/INDEX.sdd (task-scoped authority)

Navigation:
  Parent: @INDEX.sdd
  Identity: @identity.sdd
  Index: @../INDEX.sdd
  ToolGov: @../system/tool-governance.sdd

State: +
